dropped the body of system-header function
no body for callee
--
libstdc++ 13 <sstream>: `o << 4' leaves o.str() empty, without a dropped
body or a missing callee (strings and put() work).  Diagnosed (round 163v):
basic_ostream<char>::_M_insert<long> is declared `extern template' in
<ostream> (an explicit instantiation declaration, [temp.explicit]/12; the
definition, in bits/ostream.tcc, is visible), so the front end does not
instantiate its body, and provide_stdlib_bodies replaces the bodyless
instance by a model that only returns *this -- no output is inserted
([ostream.inserters.arithmetic]/1).  Without that model the call has no
body.  The same policy question as libc++'s std::sort
(cpp20_libcxx_header_drops/test_sort.desc): instantiate definitions that
are visible despite an extern template declaration.  g++ 13 accepts this
program, and it fails only its WRONG assertion.
